{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"S4 (dc0d) plan-review v1: BLOCK blocking=2, and BOTH findings were the SAME real contradiction between S4s plan and what S2 actually built — caught pre-implementation. S4 claimed capability handling comes free from S2 because an opaque endpoint resolves to the CONSERVATIVE record so structured output takes the prompted path. FALSE, verified two ways: (1) capabilities_for() reads .profile off a model OBJECT first and S4s builder produces a real OpenAIChatModel carrying the genuine OpenAI profile; (2) openai_model_profile(local-model).supports_json_schema_output is TRUE, so even the STRING path resolves through _PROFILE_RESOLVERS[openai] to a native-capable record. Either way a local Ollama/LMStudio/vLLM endpoint would get NativeOutput (strict json_schema constrained decoding) which an OpenAI-COMPATIBLE server has no obligation to implement — failure mode is a silent wrong answer or an opaque parse error. The conservative fallback never fires because a key DOES match. FIX: the builder supplies an explicit ModelProfile override — verified OpenAIChatModel.__init__ accepts profile: ModelProfileSpec|None in the pinned pydantic-ai source (same caller-supplied mechanism the epic already uses for Bedrock) — passing dataclasses.replace(openai_model_profile(name), supports_json_schema_output=False). Justification: the OpenAI profile describes OpenAIs HOSTED API; a custom base_url is by definition a DIFFERENT server that merely speaks the same wire protocol, so upstreams strict-output flag is not evidence about it. This makes the plans claim true BY CONSTRUCTION, needs no change to S2s capabilities_for, and adds no per-call boolean (preserving the rejection of PR #121s force_prompted). Added two ACs: the override is actually applied (native_structured_output False => PromptedOutput), and it is SURGICAL (another capability off the same profile is unchanged), so it cannot degenerate into a blanket conservative record."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785377044977654001,"uuid":"5ea2ca23-d20e-4897-a616-00a330076f8a"}